WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.719 --> 00:00:04.779
So this is a sample of osmium. Osmium, again,
is a precious

00:00:04.779 --> 00:00:08.040
metal, platinum-group metal, and this is an
osmium sponge

00:00:08.040 --> 00:00:11.430
which is very nicely packaged up in this box.
So let’s have a

00:00:11.430 --> 00:00:13.000
look and see if we can find it.

00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:18.539
So osmium is another one of the elements in
the so-called

00:00:18.539 --> 00:00:25.980
‘platinum group’ and it is quite unusual
in that its oxide –

00:00:25.980 --> 00:00:30.779
osmium tetroxide is a stable compound which
is really quite

00:00:30.779 --> 00:00:35.430
easily evaporated. It has quite a strong smell
which is unusual

00:00:35.430 --> 00:00:40.710
for metal compounds and it can be evaporated
quite easily

00:00:40.710 --> 00:00:46.190
and it is used in organic chemistry because
if you have

00:00:46.190 --> 00:00:49.790
compounds with double bonds between two carbon
atoms,

00:00:49.790 --> 00:00:54.650
osmium tetroxide reacts with it really quite
easily.

00:00:54.650 --> 00:01:00.180
So here the osmium itself, it is a very, very
reactive metal, it

00:01:00.180 --> 00:01:03.830
is sealed in this glass ampule under an inert
atmosphere of

00:01:03.830 --> 00:01:07.460
argon so that it can’t oxidise. The argon
is very inert and it

00:01:07.460 --> 00:01:11.580
stops the metal reacting. So here you can
see this very dark

00:01:11.580 --> 00:01:16.880
black metal, very fine spongy-type material,
at the bottom of

00:01:16.880 --> 00:01:18.930
this glass vial.

00:01:18.930 --> 00:01:24.900
Again, osmium has played some role in my life
because I did

00:01:24.900 --> 00:01:29.361
some of the early work in my doctorate involved
osmium

00:01:29.361 --> 00:01:33.010
compound, it was ruthenium and osmium and
iron. The

00:01:33.010 --> 00:01:36.680
ruthenium compound was orange, the osmium
compound a

00:01:36.680 --> 00:01:42.090
rather fetching pale yellow and the iron compound
a very dark

00:01:42.090 --> 00:01:45.799
green. And the osmium compound was perhaps
the most

00:01:45.799 --> 00:01:48.330
boring because it behaved in exactly the way
that was

00:01:48.330 --> 00:01:49.500
predicted.

00:01:49.500 --> 00:01:54.340
So osmium reacts with the air to form osmium
tetroxide,

00:01:54.340 --> 00:01:57.890
which is a very, very toxic material, it makes
us go blind so

00:01:57.890 --> 00:02:00.780
we have very careful with storing the osmium.

00:02:00.780 --> 00:02:05.320
Since then, I think in my life I have made
one osmium

00:02:05.320 --> 00:02:07.580
compound that nobody had ever made before,
it wasn’t

00:02:07.580 --> 00:02:10.950
enough to see but I could see the absorption
of light by this

00:02:10.950 --> 00:02:12.900
compound, so I was really quite excited.

00:02:12.900 --> 00:02:15.980
Do you remember what it was it in it?

00:02:15.980 --> 00:02:16.980
What?

00:02:16.980 --> 00:02:17.980
Do you remember what it was, the compound?

00:02:17.980 --> 00:02:22.290
The compound was osmium dicarbonyl dinitrosyl
and it was

00:02:22.290 --> 00:02:25.520
interesting because nobody had ever made this
compound

00:02:25.520 --> 00:02:28.520
before, but it was similar to a compound of
iron which was

00:02:28.520 --> 00:02:32.280
quite well known. The compound of iron looked
like blood; it

00:02:32.280 --> 00:02:35.150
was a really quite dramatic compound. I never
found out

00:02:35.150 --> 00:02:37.770
what the colour of the osmium compound was,
I never made

00:02:37.770 --> 00:02:39.890
enough, but I am not a very good synthetic
chemist.

